Quick backstory:
Group of childhood friends who met through their families working in the same hawker centre. Went to a hiking trip in the Greek mountains and stumbled into an ancient temple
worshipping spirits of the 4 classical elements and 3 derivative elements (Electricity to fire, life and ice to water). With the gems found in the temple, they 
gain powers to control the elements. They use their powers to run a novelty restaurant where they display their powers in the preparation of the food.

Arc 1: NightLight
2 members of the malicious Cult of the Elements found the ancient temple holding the Skia Jewel and Phos Gem, gaining the powers of umbrakinesis and photokinesis 
respectively. The cult seeks to usurp the One World Agency via control of all natural resources. Arc will take place around the Mediterranean Sea, with the original
7 Elementals fighting the 2 members Skia and Photo. Skia kills Anemo, the remaining 6 retreat. OWA is alerted of the battle and sends Arachnid, Rider and the 
Guardian of the Mist, a new character introduced in this chapter who holds the Mist Glaive and can teleport through and manipulate mist, to assist. With their combined
might they take down Skia and Photo. OWA leaves the Aero Amulet under the protection of the Elementals and offer them positions as freelance heroes, which they accept.
OWA confiscates the Skia Jewel and Photo Gem for research. It is later revealed the Guardian of the Mist is a deity within the same pantheon as the others which are 
worshipped in the temples holding the elements, and that there are temples globally worshipping various aspects of nature. Cult of the Elements mourn the loss of their
2 warriors, and start preparing for their next expedition to find the Necro Staff.

Arc 2: Shades of death
6 months after defeating Skia and Photo, the 6 have opened a restaurant in Singapore to honour Anemo. All of them still feel a deep sense of grief from Aero's death, especially
Electro, who was closest to Aero. The Cult of the Elements find the Necro Staff in Nicaragua's Masaya Volcano and defeat La Selva, a new Nicaraguan hero and inheritor of 
the Guardian's powers. The Necro Staff is given to a member and gains the nickname Grimm, who seeks to avenge Skia and Photo by killing the Elementals. However, an elder convinces
Grimm to instead manipulate the team's grief and willingly give up their gems. Grimm encounters a downtrodden Electro, and lies to him that the Skia Jewel can activate a gate to
the ancient Greek afterlife and revive Aero, but he must keep this a secret. Electro complies, breaking into an OWA compound on a day off and successfully steals the Skia Jewel.
However, when he exits near East Coast Park (a really large park in Singapore. OWA has a secret compound at the edge of the park, around 1°17'32.0"N 103°53'18.0"E), Grimm knocks
him out. The Skia Jewel begins to take over Electro's mind, and when it interacts with the Electro gem's influence on Electro, it begins to mix and bring out Electro's darker
side, a physical manifestation of Electro's grief and inner turmoil around Aero's death. This new form, "Skia-Electro", begins to unconsciously attack Grimm. Grimm uses the Necro
Staff to summon an army of skeletons and local spirits to drive off Skia-Electro, but they only push him further inland towards the Kallang (National Stadium of Singapore) where 
the Elementals were hanging out. Receiving an alert from OWA via the Rider, who took notice of the battle due to the dead being involved, the Elementals quickly went into action.
